clear-example-expected-failures (2026-08-02): eleven undiscriminated property unions across ten components, confirmed unresolvable, plus two independent generator defects out of the profile's reach. Every union was checked branch-by-branch against the vendored schema: `integration.owner`, `integration-installation-request.account`, `installation.account` and `nullable-integration.owner` are all `oneOf`/`anyOf` [simple-user, enterprise] — `simple-user` carries a `type` field but `enterprise` has none, so no field is common to both. `copilot-seat-details.assigning_team` [team, enterprise-team] and `projects-v2-item-simple.content` [issue, pull-request-simple, projects-v2-draft-issue] have the identical shape: one branch has a `type` field, the others don't. `commit.author` and `commit.committer` are [simple-user, empty-object], and `empty-object` is `properties: {}` with `additionalProperties: false` — it can never carry any field to discriminate on. `event.payload` (16 branches) and `secret-scanning-location.details` (13 branches) each have a real discriminator, but it lives on the *sibling* `type` field of the parent object, not inside the polymorphic property's own value, which is the only place a property-level `#[Discriminator]` can read from. `repository-ruleset.conditions` [repository-ruleset-conditions, org-ruleset-conditions] share only `ref_name`, itself a nested object, not a string tag. None of these eleven admits an honest `Profile::$discriminators` entry. Skipping all ten components instead was tried and independently confirmed worse: this document is deeply cross-referential, and the ten skips cascade into 231 dangling `class.notFound` PHPStan errors across unrelated models (Issue, Deployment, CheckRun, dozens of Webhook* payloads, ...) — the same no-cascade gap found on the DigitalOcean example, at ten times the blast radius, and none of the referencing operations/components can be skip-listed themselves without paogen calling the entry stale. Independently, a scalar-typed `anyOf`/`oneOf` path parameter (the same shape as DigitalOcean's `images_get`) resolves to `mixed` instead of tripping the "unsupported parameter shapes" abort, then fails PHPStan against `Endpoint::path()`'s stricter signature — 8 errors. Both are generator defects in `src/Generator/Emit/`, outside this task's file boundary — neither is fixable from the profile. The forty-nine unrelated operation-level gaps this document already had (inline JSON request bodies, unsupported query-parameter shapes, non-JSON response content types, unrepresentable response shapes) are now fully cataloged in `Profile::$skip` and verified clean on their own; only the ten discriminator components above keep this marker in place. Tracked in `clear-example-expected-failures`.
